python/src/
    driver.py                    <- THE ONE orchestrator: runs preaggregator -> aggregator -> postaggregator in sequence

    data_access/                 <- NEW shared package, used by all three EMR-stage packages
        __init__.py
        reader.py                  <- read_curated_table(name, filters) -> DataFrame  (hides Iceberg/Glue/whatever-it-ends-up-being)
        writer.py                  <- write_curated_table(df, name, mode)  (same abstraction, for writes)
        config.py                  <- catalog/connection details, the one place that changes if the underlying DB decision changes

    fileparser/                  <- unchanged, external process, not part of this EMR-workflow orchestration at all
        __init__.py
        config_parser.py
        curated_app_fact.py
        driver.py                  <- stays as-is; it's invoked independently by StoneBranch before the EMR workflow starts, not by the new top-level driver.py

    preaggregator/                <- EMR Stage 1 (lightweight validation)
        __init__.py
        run.py                     <- standalone entry point, for running just this stage in isolation
        checks/
            ...

    aggregator/                   <- EMR Stage 2 (not yet built)
        __init__.py
        run.py
        ...

    postaggregator/               <- EMR Stage 3 (what we've been calling dq_postagg)
        __init__.py
        run.py                     <- standalone entry point, for running just this stage in isolation
        checks/
            registry.py
            completeness.py
            correctness.py
            reliability.py
            coverage_lineage.py
            timeliness.py
            security_compliance.py
            structural_integrity.py
            rule1_checks.py
            rule2_checks.py
            rule3_checks.py
        results_writer.py